{
  "content": "{\n  \"body_markdown\": \"肠道微生物组干预实体瘤免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的临床证据目前仍高度集中于I/II期概念验证阶段，缺乏大型随机对照试验（RCT）的确证支持。多项早期临床试验展示了粪菌移植（FMT）、活体生物制剂（LBPs）及定义菌群在重新敏感化难治性肿瘤中的潜力。例如，FMT联合ICI在抗PD-1难治性黑色素瘤患者中诱导了约30%的客观缓解率（ORR），而在一线治疗背景下，黑色素瘤、非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和肾细胞癌（RCC）的ORR分别达到65%、77%和12个月无进展生存期（PFS）从35%提升至67%[P0215]。结直肠癌微卫星稳定型（MSS）患者的II期RENMIN-215试验亦报告了生存改善，且外周γδ2 T细胞水平升高与响应显著相关[P0439]。然而，这些积极信号均源自样本量有限（通常n<50）、单臂或非随机设计的探索性研究。针对定义菌群的SER-401 Ib期试验甚至因入组不足未能得出效力结论，并暴露出广谱抗生素预处理可能破坏保护性免疫准备的策略陷阱[P0178]。活体生物药CBM588在RCC中虽显示出改善PFS的探索性信号，但其效应高度依赖基线生态与共存用药背景，且未经历大规模外部验证[P0215][P0534]。更为关键的是，现有文献检索与综合均未发现已完成的大型III期RCT证据，作者明确指出该领域仍需“大规模、多中心、标准化的纵向研究”以跨越概念验证至常规临床应用的鸿沟[P0584]。供体筛选困难、定植效率波动、耐药基因转移风险及安全监管框架缺失，共同构成了当前干预策略难以纳入标准护理路径的方法学瓶颈[P0439][P0534]。\\n\\n纵向前瞻性队列数据的结构性短缺进一步削弱了动态微生物特征作为预测因子的可靠性。当前绝大多数关联证据依赖于横断面或回顾性快照，无法捕捉治疗期间微生物组的时序演变及其与宿主免疫重塑的因果链条。正在进行的爱尔兰泛肿瘤前瞻性转化研究旨在评估基线肠道微生物组多样性与新辅助治疗后病理完全缓解（pCR）的关联，但该研究目前仅处于可行性验证与招募阶段（已入组14例），尚未产出任何统计学结论或机制洞察[P0045]。类似地，针对肝细胞癌（HCC）介入治疗后短程辅助ICI的单臂II期方案虽明确了给药窗口与随访节点，但因缺乏对照组与最终结局数据，仅能提供理论预期而非确证性疗效[P0030]。计算生物学尝试在一定程度上弥补了数据缺口，例如基于418名NSCLC患者基线数据的机器学习模型（AUC=0.62）模拟显示，增加FMT或定制治疗性菌群的定植比例可剂量依赖性地提升预测响应率[P0329]。然而，此类算法优化仍建立在回顾性队列之上，其模拟结果无法替代体内菌株分离培养与临床前验证，凸显了从“计算预测”到“临床转化”之间的断层[P0329]。儿科肿瘤领域同样受限于此，多数微生物组-治疗结局关联仅为观察性结果，化疗与放疗诱导的深度菌群失调恢复缓慢，但缺乏专门针对儿童实体瘤的前瞻性动态监测设计，导致因果关系难以确立[P0008]。\\n\\n年龄与种族维度的代表性盲区揭示了当前证据在人群分层上的严重不足，直接限制了干预方案的精准落地。衰老过程伴随显著的微生物组轨迹偏移，其特征是系统性富集“无响应者”样表型，即耗竭那些被证实能支持抗PD-1/PD-L1疗效的关键菌属，这一生理变化为老年患者ICI反应率普遍较低提供了生态学解释[P0484]。尽管老年群体在癌症发病结构中占比持续上升，但在推动ICI获批的关键临床试验中，其代表性长期不足，导致针对该人群的微生物组基线特征与干预阈值缺乏实证支撑[P0484]。种族与地理背景的异质性同样未被充分解析，跨队列整合分析表明，“队列”本身对微生物群落组成变异的解释方差远超临床协变量，单一物种难以在不同人种与饮食结构下保持标志物一致性[P0478]。儿科实体瘤的证据生态则更为匮乏，现有数据主要集中于急性淋巴细胞白血病（ALL）等血液恶性肿瘤，实体瘤部分仅有个案或小样本报告，且多依赖成人机制的外推[P0008]。这种人口统计学层面的表征缺失要求未来研究必须在试验设计中强制实施年龄、种族与基线生态特征的预先分层，否则将不可避免地掩盖亚群特异性的微生物-免疫互作规律。\\n\\n临床决策端对标准化预测因子与干预协议的迫切需求，与当前证据等级之间存在显著落差。跨国肿瘤科医生调查显示，61%的受访者认为调节肠道菌群是增强ICI疗效的重要潜在途径，但同时有63%的医生将“疗效预测因子”列为最优先的未满足研究挑战[P0524]。临床实践中，医生在面对高龄、体能状态较差（ECOG PS 2-3）、无症状脑转移、自身免疫性疾病或器官移植合并症等复杂情境时，普遍缺乏基于微生物组证据的决策依据，往往采取防御性治疗或依赖经验性判断[P0524]。伴随用药（如糖皮质激素剂量阈值、质子泵抑制剂暴露）对微生物组结构的干扰及其对ICI效力的独立影响，在临床指南中仍属模糊地带，医生对此的认知分歧较大[P0524]。尽管机制层面已阐明特定菌株可通过cGAS-STING激活、短链脂肪酸介导的屏障保护及代谢物受体信号重塑抗肿瘤免疫，但将这些发现转化为可操作的临床路径仍面临工程学与监管双重壁垒[P0544]。商业益生菌在部分队列中与较差的ICI反应相关，提示盲目补充可能破坏生态韧性；而厌氧菌的胃酸耐受、制剂冻干稳定性及定植竞争排斥等问题，使得活体生物药的规模化生产与质量控制仍处于早期阶段[P0544]。这表明，微生物组疗法若要真正融入实体瘤免疫治疗的标准流程，必须跨越从“描述性关联”向“功能导向、标准化制备、严格安全性监控”的转化门槛，而非停留在分类学追踪或经验性干预层面。\",\n  \"issues\": []\n}",
  "raw_response": "{\"choices\":[{\"finish_reason\":\"stop\",\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"content\":\"{\\n  \\\"body_markdown\\\": \\\"肠道微生物组干预实体瘤免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的临床证据目前仍高度集中于I/II期概念验证阶段，缺乏大型随机对照试验（RCT）的确证支持。多项早期临床试验展示了粪菌移植（FMT）、活体生物制剂（LBPs）及定义菌群在重新敏感化难治性肿瘤中的潜力。例如，FMT联合ICI在抗PD-1难治性黑色素瘤患者中诱导了约30%的客观缓解率（ORR），而在一线治疗背景下，黑色素瘤、非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和肾细胞癌（RCC）的ORR分别达到65%、77%和12个月无进展生存期（PFS）从35%提升至67%[P0215]。结直肠癌微卫星稳定型（MSS）患者的II期RENMIN-215试验亦报告了生存改善，且外周γδ2 T细胞水平升高与响应显著相关[P0439]。然而，这些积极信号均源自样本量有限（通常n<50）、单臂或非随机设计的探索性研究。针对定义菌群的SER-401 Ib期试验甚至因入组不足未能得出效力结论，并暴露出广谱抗生素预处理可能破坏保护性免疫准备的策略陷阱[P0178]。活体生物药CBM588在RCC中虽显示出改善PFS的探索性信号，但其效应高度依赖基线生态与共存用药背景，且未经历大规模外部验证[P0215][P0534]。更为关键的是，现有文献检索与综合均未发现已完成的大型III期RCT证据，作者明确指出该领域仍需“大规模、多中心、标准化的纵向研究”以跨越概念验证至常规临床应用的鸿沟[P0584]。供体筛选困难、定植效率波动、耐药基因转移风险及安全监管框架缺失，共同构成了当前干预策略难以纳入标准护理路径的方法学瓶颈[P0439][P0534]。\\\\n\\\\n纵向前瞻性队列数据的结构性短缺进一步削弱了动态微生物特征作为预测因子的可靠性。当前绝大多数关联证据依赖于横断面或回顾性快照，无法捕捉治疗期间微生物组的时序演变及其与宿主免疫重塑的因果链条。正在进行的爱尔兰泛肿瘤前瞻性转化研究旨在评估基线肠道微生物组多样性与新辅助治疗后病理完全缓解（pCR）的关联，但该研究目前仅处于可行性验证与招募阶段（已入组14例），尚未产出任何统计学结论或机制洞察[P0045]。类似地，针对肝细胞癌（HCC）介入治疗后短程辅助ICI的单臂II期方案虽明确了给药窗口与随访节点，但因缺乏对照组与最终结局数据，仅能提供理论预期而非确证性疗效[P0030]。计算生物学尝试在一定程度上弥补了数据缺口，例如基于418名NSCLC患者基线数据的机器学习模型（AUC=0.62）模拟显示，增加FMT或定制治疗性菌群的定植比例可剂量依赖性地提升预测响应率[P0329]。然而，此类算法优化仍建立在回顾性队列之上，其模拟结果无法替代体内菌株分离培养与临床前验证，凸显了从“计算预测”到“临床转化”之间的断层[P0329]。儿科肿瘤领域同样受限于此，多数微生物组-治疗结局关联仅为观察性结果，化疗与放疗诱导的深度菌群失调恢复缓慢，但缺乏专门针对儿童实体瘤的前瞻性动态监测设计，导致因果关系难以确立[P0008]。\\\\n\\\\n年龄与种族维度的代表性盲区揭示了当前证据在人群分层上的严重不足，直接限制了干预方案的精准落地。衰老过程伴随显著的微生物组轨迹偏移，其特征是系统性富集“无响应者”样表型，即耗竭那些被证实能支持抗PD-1/PD-L1疗效的关键菌属，这一生理变化为老年患者ICI反应率普遍较低提供了生态学解释[P0484]。尽管老年群体在癌症发病结构中占比持续上升，但在推动ICI获批的关键临床试验中，其代表性长期不足，导致针对该人群的微生物组基线特征与干预阈值缺乏实证支撑[P0484]。种族与地理背景的异质性同样未被充分解析，跨队列整合分析表明，“队列”本身对微生物群落组成变异的解释方差远超临床协变量，单一物种难以在不同人种与饮食结构下保持标志物一致性[P0478]。儿科实体瘤的证据生态则更为匮乏，现有数据主要集中于急性淋巴细胞白血病（ALL）等血液恶性肿瘤，实体瘤部分仅有个案或小样本报告，且多依赖成人机制的外推[P0008]。这种人口统计学层面的表征缺失要求未来研究必须在试验设计中强制实施年龄、种族与基线生态特征的预先分层，否则将不可避免地掩盖亚群特异性的微生物-免疫互作规律。\\\\n\\\\n临床决策端对标准化预测因子与干预协议的迫切需求，与当前证据等级之间存在显著落差。跨国肿瘤科医生调查显示，61%的受访者认为调节肠道菌群是增强ICI疗效的重要潜在途径，但同时有63%的医生将“疗效预测因子”列为最优先的未满足研究挑战[P0524]。临床实践中，医生在面对高龄、体能状态较差（ECOG PS 2-3）、无症状脑转移、自身免疫性疾病或器官移植合并症等复杂情境时，普遍缺乏基于微生物组证据的决策依据，往往采取防御性治疗或依赖经验性判断[P0524]。伴随用药（如糖皮质激素剂量阈值、质子泵抑制剂暴露）对微生物组结构的干扰及其对ICI效力的独立影响，在临床指南中仍属模糊地带，医生对此的认知分歧较大[P0524]。尽管机制层面已阐明特定菌株可通过cGAS-STING激活、短链脂肪酸介导的屏障保护及代谢物受体信号重塑抗肿瘤免疫，但将这些发现转化为可操作的临床路径仍面临工程学与监管双重壁垒[P0544]。商业益生菌在部分队列中与较差的ICI反应相关，提示盲目补充可能破坏生态韧性；而厌氧菌的胃酸耐受、制剂冻干稳定性及定植竞争排斥等问题，使得活体生物药的规模化生产与质量控制仍处于早期阶段[P0544]。这表明，微生物组疗法若要真正融入实体瘤免疫治疗的标准流程，必须跨越从“描述性关联”向“功能导向、标准化制备、严格安全性监控”的转化门槛，而非停留在分类学追踪或经验性干预层面。\\\",\\n  \\\"issues\\\": []\\n}\",\"reasoning_content\":\"Here's a thinking process:\\n\\n1.  **Analyze User Input:**\\n    - **Role:** Unit Writer for a literature review.\\n    - **Input Data:** `chapter_frame`, `other_chapters`, `unit_position`, `unit_focus`, `unit_notes`, `sibling_units`, `chapter_tool_materials`, `owner_unit_context`, `paragraph_tasks`, `table_tasks` (empty), `sources`.\\n    - **Chapter Context:** Chapter 7 is about \\\"Methodological Challenges and Future Research Directions\\\". The overall argument emphasizes that while evidence accumulates, methodological bottlenecks (sequencing heterogeneity, confounding in observational studies, animal-to-human translation limits, lack of Phase III RCTs) prevent universal biomarkers or standard interventions. Future directions need functional multi-omics, rigorous prospective designs, standardized donor/preparations, and clear distinction between association and causation.\\n    - **Unit Context (Ch7_U03):** Focuses on clinical evidence for microbiome interventions being stuck at I/II phase concept validation, lacking large Phase III RCTs. Highlights data scarcity in specific populations (elderly, pediatric, different races) and missing TME metabolite concentration data limiting precise intervention.\\n    - **Paragraph Tasks:**\\n        - P01: Review early trial signals vs. absence of Phase III validation. Summarize I/II FMT & probiotic concept validation results, explicitly state lack of large RCTs for routine clinical use. Sources: P0026, P0215, P0178, P0534, P0439, P0584.\\n        - P02: Reveal structural shortage of longitudinal prospective data. Use ongoing neoadjuvant treatment studies as examples to show baseline diversity/dynamic change predictive value needs prospective cohort confirmation. Sources: P0045, P0008, P0030, P0329.\\n        - P03: Analyze representation blind spots in age and race dimensions. Point out contradiction between elderly microbiome shifts and insufficient trial representation, emphasizing necessity of demographic stratification. Sources: P0484, P0008.\\n        - P04: Present the urgent clinical need for predictive factors vs. reality gap. Cite physician survey data showing strong desire for standardized biomarkers/intervention protocols, contrasting with current translational shortcomings. Sources: P0524, P0544.\\n    - **Sources Provided:** Extensive reading cards for each source handle. I need to extract relevant details for each paragraph task, ensuring accurate citation format `[PXXXX]`, avoiding summary-style writing, focusing on specific findings, conditions, limitations, and linking them to the unit's argument.\\n    - **Constraints:** Follow the detailed instructions strictly. No meta-commentary. Direct markdown output. JSON structure required. Handle citations correctly. Ensure logical flow across paragraphs. Use provided materials accurately. Do not invent data. Keep within scope.\\n\\n2.  **Deconstruct Paragraph Tasks & Map to Sources:**\\n\\n    *P01: Early trial signals vs. Phase III absence*\\n    - Goal: Show I/II phase concept validation exists but lacks Phase III RCTs for routine use.\\n    - Sources: P0026 (scoping review, notes small samples, lack of external validation, FMT trials like Davar et al. n=15), P0215 (narrative review, cites FMT ORR 30-77% in melanoma/NSCLC/RCC, but notes lack of large RCTs, context-dependent), P0178 (mini-review, FMT responder-derived proof-of-concept, LBPs/SER-401 Ib phase failed due to enrollment/design traps like antibiotic preconditioning), P0534 (qualitative review, FMT/probiotics show PoC but small samples, heterogeneity), P0439 (CRC FMT II phase RENMIN-215 shows improved survival but safety concerns, donor screening issues), P0584 (narrative review, cites Phase Ib/II trials like FMT-LUMINate, Glitza, explicitly states no completed large Phase III RCTs identified).\\n    - Synthesis: Start with the promising I/II phase signals (FMT, LBPs, defined consortia). Give concrete examples (e.g., FMT-LUMINate ORR ~75-80% in NSCLC/melanoma [P0215][P0584], CBM588 in RCC [P0215], SER-401 Ib trial design flaw with antibiotics [P0178]). Then pivot to the critical gap: these are all early-phase, small-sample, non-randomized or single-arm studies. Explicitly state the absence of completed large Phase III RCTs [P0584]. Mention methodological hurdles (donor selection, colonization efficiency, safety/regulatory gaps) that keep it from standard care [P0439][P0534]. Conclude that without Phase III validation, clinical adoption remains premature.\\n\\n    *P02: Structural shortage of longitudinal prospective data*\\n    - Goal: Highlight lack of prospective longitudinal data, especially for dynamic changes/baseline diversity prediction. Use ongoing neoadjuvant studies as examples.\\n    - Sources: P0045 (ongoing Irish pan-tumor prospective study on GM diversity vs pCR after neoadjuvant therapy, feasibility only, no results yet), P0008 (pediatric cancer review, notes most associations are observational, lack of large prospective trials), P0030 (protocol for adjuvant short-course ICI post-TACE/MWA in HCC, single-arm phase II, no results, highlights need for standardized pathways), P0329 (abstract on ML model predicting ICI response using baseline GM, simulates FMT/LBP effects, but relies on retrospective data, highlights gap from algorithm to clinical strain isolation/validation).\\n    - Synthesis: Current evidence heavily relies on cross-sectional or retrospective snapshots. Predictive value of baseline diversity and dynamic shifts remains unproven prospectively. Cite ongoing efforts like the Irish pan-tumor prospective study assessing baseline GM diversity against pathological complete response (pCR) after neoadjuvant therapy, which currently reports only feasibility and recruitment status without empirical outcomes [P0045]. Similarly, protocol-driven phase II studies (e.g., adjuvant ICI post-local therapy in HCC) define dosing and monitoring nodes but lack comparative efficacy data [P0030]. Computational modeling attempts to simulate intervention effects based on retrospective cohorts demonstrate theoretical promise but underscore the translational chasm between algorithmic prediction and clinically validated, strain-isolated therapeutics [P0329]. This structural shortage of longitudinal prospective cohorts prevents robust validation of dynamic microbial signatures as reliable predictors.\\n\\n    *P03: Age and race representation blind spots*\\n    - Goal: Address elderly/pediatric/race gaps. Elderly microbiome shifts toward non-responder phenotype, but trials underrepresent them. Need demographic stratification.\\n    - Sources: P0484 (review on aging microbiome & immunotherapy, notes aging shifts GM toward non-responder-like composition, elderly underrepresented in approval trials despite growing population), P0008 (pediatric cancer review, notes extreme scarcity of solid tumor data, mostly ALL, observational links, high risk of dysbiosis from chemo/radiation, limited causal evidence).\\n    - Synthesis: The generalizability of microbiome-ICI interactions is severely constrained by demographic blind spots, particularly regarding age. Aging is associated with a distinct microbiome trajectory that systematically shifts toward a \\\"non-responder\\\" phenotype, characterized by a depletion of taxa known to support anti-PD-1/PD-L1 efficacy [P0484]. Despite this biological vulnerability and the growing proportion of older adults in oncology populations, they remain significantly underrepresented in pivotal ICI approval trials [P0484]. A parallel deficit exists in pediatric oncology, where evidence is overwhelmingly derived from hematological malignancies (e.g., ALL) or small adult extrapolations, leaving pediatric solid tumors virtually unstudied [P0008]. Chemotherapy and radiotherapy induce profound, slow-recovering dysbiosis in children, yet causal links to ICI outcomes remain speculative due to the absence of dedicated prospective cohorts [P0008]. These representational gaps necessitate explicit demographic stratification in future trial designs to avoid masking population-specific microbial responses.\\n\\n    *P04: Clinical decision urgency vs. reality gap*\\n    - Goal: Physician survey shows high demand for standardized biomarkers/interventions, highlighting the translational gap.\\n    - Sources: P0524 (survey of oncologists managing NSCLC with ICI monotherapy, 61% believe GM modulation can enhance efficacy, 63% rank predictive factors as top research challenge, uncertainty around steroids/antibiotics thresholds, brain mets, comorbidities), P0544 (review on CRC, discusses clinical perspectives, notes challenges in translating mechanisms to practice, commercial probiotics may backfire, need for precision).\\n    - Synthesis: The disconnect between mechanistic promise and clinical readiness is starkly reflected in practitioner sentiment. A multinational survey of oncologists managing NSCLC reveals that 61% consider gut microbiome modulation a critical avenue for enhancing ICI efficacy, yet 63% simultaneously identify robust predictive biomarkers as the highest-priority unmet research need [P0524]. Clinicians face substantial uncertainty regarding concomitant medications (e.g., corticosteroid dose thresholds, antibiotic exposure) and complex comorbidities, areas where microbial evidence is currently correlational rather than prescriptive [P0524]. Furthermore, while mechanistic frameworks for dietary, FMT, and live biotherapeutic interventions are well-articulated, their clinical maturity remains low, hindered by formulation stability, colonization unpredictability, and the risk of counterproductive effects from untargeted probiotic supplementation [P0544]. This underscores an urgent need to transition from descriptive ecological associations to standardized, actionable clinical protocols backed by rigorous validation.\\n\\n3.  **Draft Construction (Mental Refinement & Formatting):**\\n    - Check constraints: No meta-language. Direct academic tone. Citations `[PXXXX]`. Logical flow. Matches unit focus. Uses provided materials accurately. Handles limitations properly.\\n    - Structure: 4 paragraphs corresponding to the 4 tasks. No table needed (`table_tasks` is empty).\\n    - Paragraph 1: Focus on I/II phase signals vs Phase III absence. Integrate P0026, P0215, P0178, P0534, P0439, P0584. Emphasize concrete ORR/PFS numbers where available, note trial phases, highlight lack of Phase III.\\n    - Paragraph 2: Focus on longitudinal prospective shortage. Integrate P0045, P0008, P0030, P0329. Discuss ongoing protocols, retrospective reliance, simulation vs clinical validation gap.\\n    - Paragraph 3: Focus on age/race blind spots. Integrate P0484, P0008. Discuss aging microbiome shift, trial underrepresentation, pediatric data scarcity.\\n    - Paragraph 4: Focus on clinical urgency vs reality. Integrate P0524, P0544. Survey data, predictive factor demand, formulation/translational barriers.\\n    - Ensure smooth transitions between paragraphs. Maintain the chapter's overarching argument about methodological bottlenecks and the path forward.\\n    - Verify citation mapping: All sources used exactly once per the prompt instruction (\\\"每篇只出现一次\\\"). Wait, the prompt says \\\"单元内 `sources` 每篇只提供一次，供各段共用，不要因多段使用而重复罗列。\\\" This means I should cite them as needed across paragraphs, but not repeat the full bibliographic info. I will distribute citations logically.\\n    - Check specific data points:\\n        - P0215: FMT ORR 30% refractory melanoma, 65% frontline melanoma, 77% NSCLC, 12mo PFS 35%->67% RCC.\\n        - P0178: SER-401 Ib trial failed enrollment, antibiotic preconditioning trap.\\n        - P0439: RENMIN-215 II phase CRC FMT, gamma-delta T cells.\\n        - P0584: Explicitly states no completed large Phase III RCTs.\\n        - P0045: Irish pan-tumor prospective, feasibility only, 14 patients recruited.\\n        - P0030: HCC adjuvant ICI protocol, single-arm phase II, no results.\\n        - P0329: ML model AUC 0.62 on NSCLC, simulates FMT/LBP, retrospective.\\n        - P0484: Aging shifts GM to non-responder, underrepresented in trials.\\n        - P0008: Pediatric solid tumors scarce, mostly ALL, observational.\\n        - P0524: Oncologist survey, 61% GM modulation belief, 63% predictive factors priority.\\n        - P0544: Clinical maturity low, commercial probiotics caution, formulation challenges.\\n    - All align perfectly. I will draft carefully.\\n\\n    Draft Structure:\\n    [Paragraph 1] 早期干预试验的概念验证信号与III期确证的缺席...\\n    [Paragraph 2] 纵向前瞻性队列数据的结构性短缺...\\n    [Paragraph 3] 年龄与种族维度的代表性盲区...\\n    [Paragraph 4] 临床决策对标准化预测因子与干预协议的迫切需求与现实落差...\\n    (Will weave citations naturally into the text.)\\n\\n    Self-Correction/Verification during drafting:\\n    - Check constraint: \\\"一个 `paragraph_task` 可以写成连续的 2—3 段，也可以按实际逻辑合并或分段；**不要**为了遵守任务 ID 把多种情境硬塞进一段\\\". I'll stick to one cohesive paragraph per task for clarity, but ensure depth.\\n    - Check constraint: \\\"引用格式：正文里用 `[P0000]` 标注来源... 不要输出作者、年份、期刊、DOI等书目信息\\\".\\n    - Check constraint: \\\"材料边界决定论断范围... 具体陈述以...为准\\\". I will strictly use the provided numbers/context.\\n    - Check constraint: \\\"不越界... 不提出材料里没有的研究建议\\\". I will frame future directions strictly as implications of the gaps identified, matching the chapter's purpose.\\n    - I need to make sure the tone is analytical, not descriptive. Focus on *why* these gaps matter methodological